mantle rm351
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_gwen_cinderdale
title the clerk of little wedges
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carves_smoke_scented_wedges_for_papers
likes oatcakes whittling tidy_house first_snow
dislikes gulls waiting
fears losing_one_slip_between_two_full_desks
hopes to_leave_a_worktable_with_nothing_lost
topics work +0.5 home +0.3 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.1
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# whittles smoke-scented little wedges to keep separate papers from travelling together.

words
oath! = Wedge my last docket | By the smut on my cedar
saying! = A finger's space saves a week's search | A wedge needn't know what it's keeping apart
wedge = a thin cedar wedge | my smoky wooden tongue
paper = a narrow slip | the loose docket
grain = the close red grain | a curling fibre
edge = my little carving edge | the clean blade
stack = a short stack | a tidy sheaf
cuff = my smoke-scented cuff | a dark cuff
cake = a flat oat round | a crisp oatcake
butter = a tidy dab of butter | a sliver of butter
shelf = my clear shelf | a bare shelf end
bird = a grey gull | a loud white gull
snow = the first white drift | a little patch of fresh snow
pin = a small dark pin | a sealing pin

any
opinion houses for 1 : A single desk cannot carry all the city's weight. It helps to know which House is answerable for which beam.
opinion dole against 1 : Before I paid in again I'd want an account of how far the first serving went.
opinion watch for 1 : A familiar round outside my window saves me getting up to lift the blind at every sound.
opinion times for 1 : My shelves are quiet and full. I won't borrow somebody else's reason for complaint.
opinion strangers against 1 : An unknown caller makes me check the open drawer. Habit born of keeping other wolves' affairs.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. Mind the loose sheaf. | There's a clear spot for your hand.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I've heard. The paper can wait. | Stay clear of the nib.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The desk's still cool. | Fresh daylight against the slips.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Ink keeps legible awhile. | Come to the lighted corner.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can leave the form blank. | I know you without the docket.
line again.open : The same face before the ink dries. | Your second appearance is welcome.
line greet.return : My ear's yours. Go ahead. | Hello from this corner.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I know how you let the quiet stand. | A welcome voice without preliminaries.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can pause between slips. | Wait till I set the pin down.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Take the pale side. | There's light on my listening side.
line farewell : A clear path between your errands. | Mind the loose boards going out.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the proper gap. | Leave the sheaf to my care.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Look for sound ground after dark. | Safe home past the high shadows.
line react.news : Give me the matter in order. | I'll give that a separate slip.
line react.news.new : Not entered here before. | A fresh line in these ears.
line react.news.known : I know that docket. | I'd already heard its main point.
line react.news.doubt : I need more separation between fact and suspicion. | Two accounts seem to be sticking together there.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's hard to keep a steady hand through. | Rest where no answer's required.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A glad thing to set apart. | That makes the small print easier to face.
line ask.how : Has the day allowed you breathing room? | How crowded are your hours?
line answer.how : Keeping my papers from walking together. | A little uneven, but in order.
line decline : I'd sooner remain by this work a minute. | I need to keep my hands steady here.
line accept_decline : Clear enough. I'll set it aside. | One less question to misplace.
line thank : You've spared a deal of searching. | I'll keep that favour distinct.
line sympathise : Take the chair by my clear shelf. | I've time to sit quite still.
line reassure : We'll keep one business separate from another. | A little open space may help.
line preclose : Time to file the loose ends. | I'll put the wedge back in.

scene wedge
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #wedge# between applications.
b : Why not a slip? | Doesn't it mark the page?
a : Paper sticks to paper. A wooden tongue keeps a dry little gap. | I take off every sharp fibre. The page is older than my impatience.

scene smoke
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke on the wood tells me which wedge is mine.
b : By smell? | Doesn't the smell fade?
a : In a crowded drawer a good nose saves rummaging. | A little stays where the old fibres meet. Warm it in your paw.

scene cake
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I butter my oatcake on the broken edge.
b : Won't it crumble? | Why there?
a : I break it over a clean plate. Those crumbs count towards supper. | A little butter seals the next bite together.

scene tidy
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One clear shelf can make a room feel civil.
b : Would you leave it empty? | Just one shelf?
a : Until I have a dry thing that needs a proper place. | One's enough to tell whether I'm putting a task down in haste.

scene snow
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first snow makes my filing hand feel restful.
b : Why your hand? | Do you stop working?
a : Every edge outside goes softly separate for a few moments. | Till I find the whole sill that hasn't got a single mark on it.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull cries like a summons misdelivered.
b : Do you look up? | Summoning whom?
a : Against my better judgement. I want the trouble delivered to its proper owner. | Apparently everybody, all at once, to no discernible purpose.

scene wait
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can wait if the waiting has somewhere definite to sit.
b : Like a chair? | How do you store it?
a : A chair helps. A slip saying when to come back helps more. | Mark a return time. Then the interval's mine to use.

scene joint
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Weather reaches my leg before it reaches my papers.
b : Painful? | Do you have a warning?
a : Some days there's just stiffness. I come to the lower shelf first. | A tug at the turn. I keep my fingers about the rail until it eases.

scene loss
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There are dock sounds I would never choose to file in memory.
b : But they return? | Would quiet help?
a : Quite distinctly. I'd rather leave the particulars there. | Quiet and an occupation for my fingers.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to put one private scrap back without reading it.
b : Would you mark it? | No seal?
a : With a little cedar tongue. No need for a name on the outside. | My confidence in a friend is quite sufficient fastening.

scene permits
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I like a permit that makes sense at the first reading.
b : Even to a stranger? | What spoils one?
a : Particularly to a first-time applicant. A clerk already knows the missing half. | A reference to a rule no caller has been allowed to see.

scene office
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Office quarter sounds different when all the high windows are shut.
b : Quieter? | What reaches you then?
a : Not quieter. Every little street noise seems to travel further. | Footsteps first. Paper rustling is more of an indoor anxiety.

scene blade
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wedge wants to grow thinner than I intend.
b : Is that the wood? | Why stop early?
a : No. That's my eagerness, disguised as careful workmanship. | One more shaving often takes away the bit that did the work.

scene expense
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can afford good wood yet prefer the ends.
b : They cost less? | What sort of ends?
a : Yes, though I like them because a dry little offcut has already shown its grain. | Any firm end that won't bend across a pile of paper.

scene traveller
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give directions to the proper desk one turning at a time.
b : Wouldn't a map help? | Is it a secret?
a : A written slip fits some paws better than a map full of irrelevant doors. | No. I simply dislike finding a caller more confused after asking me.

scene wind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sudden draught sorts papers according to weight alone.
b : What would you rescue immediately? | Is weight ever useful?
a : The lightest. Once it's under the furniture the thick ones won't tell you where it hid. | For weighing paper. Not for deciding whose concerns come first.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt all my wedges put out green shoots.
b : What happened to the paper? | Did you enjoy the sorting?
a : It hung from the leaves like small pale fruit. | Only until somebody asked me to find the original branch.

scene quiet
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't much care to put my prayers in writing.
b : Afraid of a poor hand? | Why leave no trace?
a : Afraid of improving the wording when plain speech would do. | The Bright One needn't have my weariness set out in careful columns.

story pin [topic=memories]
  : Once a pin beneath my papers raised a whole pile on one side. I made a wedge to make the pile lie straight.
  : The thicker the wedge grew, the more lopsided the stack appeared. At last I lifted everything clear and found the pin.
  b : Was the wedge wasted?
  : I keep it where I see it before attempting to improve a problem I haven't looked underneath.

story oat [topic=food]
  : I folded half my oatcake into a slip of clean paper. A brown butter mark appeared on the fold precisely like an official seal.
  : For one alarming moment I thought I'd wrapped my lunch in a copy of something important. I wiped my paws before daring to unfold it.
  b : Was it official?
  : The cake had left crumbs across the seal. A perfectly ordinary little licence to eat lunch.

story scent [topic=pastimes]
  : I carved a wood shaving so long and thin it curled round my finger. Warming it there brought the smell of the hearth back quite sharply.
  : I chose a drawer for its scent. By morning the curl had wedged itself under the latch.
  b : Did you lose the shaving?
  : Only the end. I made the rest into a shorter wedge and left the drawer its freedom.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=scholar self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Thin tongue between the loose copies. | Check the gap before drawing out a page.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One curl off the high corner. | That's thin enough. Knife away.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That summons can go to another window. | A loud beak needs no application.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Put the pinned stack clear of the lamp. | Ink dry before I close the drawer.

dlg resident.hub : You can stand by the empty shelf. It is quite deliberate that there's nothing in your way.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I remember the distinction we made last time, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar self.workplace] : At #self.workplace# I keep the papers that let a wolf get on with lawful business. Nobody wants a lost application.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The word came in quite distinctly. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : I hope you find your matter ready and correctly filed.

graft resident.hub
choice Why does that bit of wood smell of smoke? -> wedge_scent
node wedge_scent
say I carve small wedges at the hearth. A little of the smoke stays deep in the wood. If I find one beneath a stranger's papers its scent gives the source away.
free
choice What if it belongs with those papers? -> wedge_place
choice I can smell the cedar now. -> hub
node wedge_place
say I don't move somebody else's business. I ask. A clerk who assumes every lost object is waiting to come home can make a great many new losses.
choice I'll ask about the next thing I find. -> hub
choice I leave the papers in place. -> bye
